{
  "_comment": "Message fragmentation. A message is UTF-8 text; fragments are [kind][payload], at most max_fragment_bytes (16384 unless stated) including the kind byte: kind 0 whole message, 1 more follows, 2 last. A message that fits one fragment is kind 0, otherwise the payload is cut every max_fragment_bytes - 1 bytes (inside a character if need be). Messages are given as {text} or {prefix?, unit, count, suffix?} = prefix + unit repeated count times + suffix; fragments are checked by length and SHA-256 (hex given when short). The receiver rejects: an empty fragment, a fragment above 16384 bytes, an unknown kind, kind 2 without a preceding kind 1, kind 0 during a split message, more than 16777216 bytes of message, and invalid UTF-8 after reassembly. A fragment too big to inline is given as {recipe: {kind, payload_length, fill_hex}} = the kind byte followed by payload_length copies of the fill byte. Generated by test/gen-remote-fixtures.mjs.",
